# The DIM=8 ASYMMETRIC MX tests (8x8 widen mesh): different-format activation x weight, BF16 output.
# DIM=8 port of asym_dim32.jobs. These live in the bareMetalC ISA suite; simq resolves the names against
# build_mx_rocket/bareMetalC/<name>-baremetal.
#
#   sim/simq run CONFIG=MxDim8AllAsymGemminiRocketConfig BINARY=baremetal/mxgemmini/asym_dim8.jobs JOBS=8
#
# IMPORTANT: run under CONFIG=MxDim8AllAsymGemminiRocketConfig (the 8x8 all-format asym mesh, all-bf16 acc).
# Build the ELFs first: ../../software/gemmini-rocc-tests/build_mx_rocket.sh bareMetalC
# Goldens: gen_asym.py --dim 8 (precision_for_dim(8) = all bf16), unified DIM-aware / Spike-consistent.
# Tests: copied from the *_dim32 asym tests, only #define DIM 8 + the _dim8 golden include changed.
#

